[1.1.7]

- Update windmill 1.792.2 -> 1.801.0
- Security: multiple cross-workspace isolation fixes preventing data, code and configuration leakage between workspaces; token scope and lifetime hardening to prevent privilege escalation and unauthorised access; path traversal and input validation fixes on file sync, MCP endpoints and error handler routing
- Breaking: MCP script tool split into createScript and updateScript; filesystem workspace storage removed from non-debug builds; Slack resource-connect OAuth migrated to v2; service log storage migrated to columnar parquet with day-partitioned index; AI skills are now per-workspace resources requiring explicit selection; ephemeral job token lifetime bounded to job timeout
- New data model for AI agent evals (datasets, scored runs, comparison); token cost tracking in AI sessions and chats; fork subscription prevention with unified seat counting
- No packaging changes: auth topology, workspace layout and secrets handling unchanged; base and built images digest-pinned

[1.1.6]
* Windmill 1.792.2 (from 1.783.0), thirteen upstream releases
* Security: ansible git repository URLs are validated before git is invoked (1.792.2)
* Schema: 1.790.0 adds a `trigger_history` table with source tracking, so this update carries a database migration
* No breaking changes and no environment variable, config path or port changes across the span

[1.1.5]
* Upstream Windmill 1.782.0 to 1.783.0. Thirteen commits, no database migrations.
* New user-visible feature: an opt-in public sharing option for job pages, guarded by
  Windmill's own authentication layer and shipped with new read-auth tests upstream. Sharing
  remains off unless a user enables it per job page.
* Fixes include scoping a forked workspace's cloned app policy and custom path to its creator.
* Package validation: full survival leg on staging (install 1.1.4 from the published feed,
  update over live data, restore from a named backup, data byte-identical at every stage) and
  the running binary verified to report v1.783.0 after deploy.

[1.1.4]
* Upstream Windmill 1.777.1 to 1.782.0 (6 releases). Adds Azure Workload Identity support for
  mssql and postgres connections, and improved database authentication logging. Removes the tag
  management UI and app staticOutputs.
* One schema migration lands with this bump (workspace_diff_last_event). Verified over a populated
  store: 621 applied migrations became 622, every row count identical before and after, and a
  restore from a named backup returned the same data byte for byte.
* Known divergence, recorded rather than silently adopted: upstream added CA-certificate
  auto-registration and an INIT_SCRIPT pre-flight hook to its own entrypoint. This package's
  start.sh carries neither.

[1.1.3]
* Upstream Windmill 1.776.0 to 1.777.1 (3 releases). Fixes include sandboxed-container job results
  (result.json/stdout) returning correctly again, and a vite revert that stops random 500 error
  pages in the UI. Features: a dedicated dbt editor with a refreshed model graph, session recording
  in app dev, and an on-behalf-of badge on script/flow pages.
* One schema migration lands with this bump (dbt editor preview graphs): it relaxes a NOT NULL so
  editor-buffer graphs can exist without a deployed version, and adds versioned/editor indexes.
  Applied automatically on first boot, as usual.

[1.1.2]
* Upstream Windmill 1.741.0 to 1.776.0 (44 releases). No packaging change: the Cloudron layer copies the same six binaries from the official image, so upstream's own base move (Debian bookworm to trixie) and their build-tool bumps do not reach this image. Includes upstream's fix for an unauthenticated DAP debugger launch bypass.
* Windmill applies its own schema migrations on boot; 35 new ones land with this bump. Two drop a redundant column each (azure_trigger.email, workspace_settings.deploy_to) after folding the surviving data forward — deploy_to links that could not be converted are preserved in a workspace_deploy_to_unmigrated table rather than discarded.

[1.1.1]
* Documentation/metadata only (same application image as 1.1.0). Label the package clearly as an unofficial community package — not affiliated with or endorsed by Windmill Labs — and scoped as a single-node, small-team deployment. No functional change.

[1.1.0]
* Topology: run Windmill as a dedicated API/UI server process plus one or more dedicated worker processes under supervisor, instead of MODE=standalone (which upstream supports for development only, with NUM_WORKERS pinned to 1). This is the same server/worker split Windmill ships in its docker-compose, co-located in the single Cloudron container.
* Worker count scales with the app's memory limit (Cloudron → Resources): more memory means more worker processes, sized to leave headroom for PostgreSQL and the server. Override with the WINDMILL_WORKER_COUNT environment variable.
* No data, settings, or credentials change; existing installs keep their database and caches and migrate in place. Security posture is unchanged — native jobs run in the app's trust boundary; nsjail / PID-namespace isolation remain unavailable under Cloudron's unprivileged container.

[1.0.2]
* Add packagerName/packagerUrl to the manifest. Cloudron 9.x rejects a community install when packagerName is empty, so the versions-URL install failed. Metadata-only fix — same application image as 1.0.1.

[1.0.1]
* Bundled PostgreSQL data directory moved to a Cloudron persistentDir (/app/pgdata), excluded from the filesystem backup.
* Added a logical-dump backup strategy (backupCommand/restoreCommand) using pg_dumpall so backups are consistent — a hot file-copy of a running Postgres data directory is unsafe (torn pages). Existing installs migrate the cluster automatically on first boot.
* Postgres major-version guard: refuse to start (no silent re-init) if the data directory version does not match the bundled server; documents the pg_upgrade path.
* Conservative Postgres memory settings (shared_buffers/work_mem) for the shared container memory budget; documented a recommended memory floor.

[1.0.0]
* Initial release of Windmill for Cloudron.
* Windmill Community Edition 1.741.0, official binary used unmodified.
* Single container: Windmill standalone (server + worker) + bundled PostgreSQL 16 + nginx, under supervisor.
* All state under /app/data (PostgreSQL data, dependency caches), captured by Cloudron backups.
* Outgoing email wired to the Cloudron sendmail addon.
* Languages out of the box: Python (uv), TypeScript (Deno/Bun), Go, Bash, SQL.
* App-native authentication; optionalSso.
